{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>et My statutes, etc.; your animal, etc.</b> In Torat Kohanim they said, and this is their language: ״I have only his own animal; from where do I derive another's animal? It is derived: 'et My statutes'״ — thus far. And it is difficult: if so, why did the verse need to say <b>your animal</b>? It should have said ״a animal you shall not breed as a mixture,״ and then it would not have needed to include others' animals. And I saw that the master, the author of Korban Aharon, wrote on this that the verse speaks in the present tense. And his words do not appear correct to me, for it would not speak in the present tense in a place where there is room for error, and would need to add words to remove the error." "<b>And it appears</b> to note the order of the verses: why did the verse juxtapose the commandment of breeding to the commandment of love of fellow man? And who knows to arrange an arrangement as fitting as HaShem our Elohim. Indeed, inasmuch as HaShem commanded concerning love of friends and the bonding of their hearts together, for HaShem desires the bonding of the branches of holiness, from this a person might say that HaShem would not object to breeding pure with pure. Therefore the verse came and said that the desire is not for this — to bond animal with animal, even within two branches of purity, even though both are of the category of purity. And therefore it was precise to say ״your animal,״ meaning an animal that is pure for you for eating. And you will find that in Torat Kohanim they expounded, and this is their language: ״I have only animal with animal; pure with impure, impure with pure — from where? It is derived: 'et My statutes you shall keep'״ — thus far. See that the Tanna holds that ״your animal״ is a pure animal, and if the verse had not said ״your animal״ I would not have known that the pure is included; and on the contrary, the act would be permitted, inasmuch as it is a bonding of a category of purity, and even if HaShem had added some inclusion, I would have expounded it regarding one of the other mixtures of impure and pure."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:18.604627895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}